            "essentialcraft5:fancy_mru_tiles",
            "essentialcraft5:fancy_mru_futuristic_tile",
            "essentialcraft5:fancy_mru_machine",
            "essentialcraft5:fancy_mru_runic",
            "essentialcraft5:fancy_mru_nether_star",
            "essentialcraft5:fancy_mru_plate",
            "essentialcraft5:fancy_mru_packed_plate",
            "essentialcraft5:fancy_mru_double_plate",
            "essentialcraft5:fancy_mru_gem"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "tip",
          "style": "good",
          "title": "Done when",
          "text": "You are holding your first patterned block."
        },
        {
          "type": "tip",
          "style": "info",
          "title": "Choosing a pattern",
          "text": "The simplest are the Runic, Star, Plated and Packet Plated Tiles, where 8 Big Tiles around one item give 8. The costliest is the Tile With Gear, which needs Ancient Big Tiles and Fancy Tiles first, and then Futuristic Tiles made from them."
        },
        {
          "type": "tip",
          "style": "warn",
          "title": "Watch out",
          "text": "Patterned blocks <w>can't be turned back</w> into their base, and they can't stand in for it in other recipes or multiblocks. The [[enrichment/controller]] shell and the [[tesla/mru_coil]] base won't accept them, so keep enough base blocks aside before you chisel."
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Each block drops itself when broken. The stone ones need a pickaxe, while Fancy Cold Stone breaks by hand. Placing and breaking them follows the same rules as any ordinary block."
        }
      ]
