        "essentialcraft5:fancy_mimic_tiles",
        "essentialcraft5:fancy_mimic_futuristic_tile",
        "essentialcraft5:fancy_mimic_machine",
        "essentialcraft5:fancy_mimic_runic",
        "essentialcraft5:fancy_mimic_nether_star",
        "essentialcraft5:fancy_mimic_plate",
        "essentialcraft5:fancy_mimic_packed_plate",
        "essentialcraft5:fancy_mimic_double_plate",
        "essentialcraft5:fancy_mimic_gem"
      ],
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "<em>Goal</em> (optional): make Fancy Mimic Blocks. They are a <em>solid</em> version of the [[automation/mimic]], and once disguised, they show their pattern over the block they copy."
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "<em>Prepare</em>: a {item:essentialcraft5:mimic} and the chisel in a crafting grid give 4 {item:essentialcraft5:fancy_mimic_big_tile}. For the other patterns, follow the tree in [[decorations/patterns]]."
        },
        {
          "type": "recipe",
          "item": "essentialcraft5:fancy_mimic_big_tile"
        },
        {
          "type": "h",
          "text": "How to use it"
        },
        {
          "type": "steps",
          "items": [
            "Right-click it with a block and it takes on that block's look, with the pattern on top. The block in your hand isn't used up.",
            "To change the look, right-click it again with another block.",
            "Sneak and right-click with both hands empty to reset it."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "tip",
          "style": "good",
          "title": "Done when",
          "text": "After disguising it, the pattern shows on the copied block and you bump into it when you walk up."
        },
        {
          "type": "h",
          "text": "How it differs from the Mimic Block"
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "<em>It is solid</em>: players and mobs can't pass through. Its hitbox follows the disguise, half a block tall as a slab and a full block when undisguised, and looking like a ladder doesn't make it climbable.",
            "The pattern is always drawn over the disguise, so it's easy to tell from the real block.",
            "Everything else works as for the Mimic Block. It can't copy Mimic Blocks, Fancy Mimic Blocks, block entities such as chests, fluids or barriers. It blocks light whatever it looks like, mobs don't spawn in or on it, and its disguise can't be changed in Adventure mode."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "tip",
          "style": "info",
          "title": "Which one to use",
          "text": "For secret doors and hidden machines, use the plain Mimic Block. It has no collision, so it looks like a wall but you walk straight through. The Fancy Mimic Block is solid, good for laying out patterns from other blocks' looks and for walls that are plainly decorative."
        },
        {
          "type": "tip",
          "style": "lore",
          "text": "The original research book mentions it only in passing, on the Mimic Block page, saying the plain one has no collision and the fancy one does."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
